      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T15:00:00Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the exploit receipt and full call trace, all five Ethereum Pool creation transactions and CREATE2 traces, verified-contract metadata, runtime code at each deployment block and immediately before exploitation, and KyberSwap's post-mortem. The successful anchor at block 18630392 index 41 is sent by KyberSwap's confirmed primary-exploiter address and repeatedly executes the vulnerable swap sequence against pools 0xfd7b111aa83b9b6f547e617c7601efd997f64703, 0xfbc887823dd414edf76c5da88ffcd9eef2ba87cc, 0x36240069ff26cecbde04d9e49a2af8d39146263e, 0x93fc0acf77edd68e611f8a776c9995f350f84274, and 0x35e6f409565a98500001783ea090e6f669744c83. Etherscan identifies each 24,229-byte direct runtime as Pool compiled with Solidity 0.8.9. Each deployment trace shows factory 0xc7a590291e07b9fe9e64b86c58fd8fc764308c4a creating the recorded address with CREATE2, and every deployment-block runtime hash equals its pre-exploit hash. These immutable non-proxy pools therefore age from their individual deployments. The post-mortem identifies the double-rounding current-tick/base-liquidity mismatch and reports $55,234,535.17 taken across the campaign before recoveries."
    }
